<title>GERMANY: Rewe buys Metro food wholesale unit.</title>
<headline>Rewe buys Metro food wholesale unit.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German retailer Rewe AG said on Tuesday it had acquired food wholesaler BLV-Grossverbraucher Service from Swiss-controlled stores group Metro AG.</p>
<p>Purchase terms were not disclosed, but the transaction has already been approved by German cartel authorities.</p>
<p>Rewe said in a statement that BLV, which supplies large-scale food consumers, had annual turnover of 400 million marks ($256.2 million) and employed 500 staff.</p>
<p>BLV will be integrated into Rewe's wholly-owned wholesale unit Rewe-Wibu, which has annual turnover of 580 million marks.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150 ($ = 1.561 German Marks)</p>
</text>
